# Space Travel — demo timeline. Dev builds reload this file when it is saved.
#
#   scene     duration  [transition [length]]  [key=value ...]
#
# duration / length: seconds (7.5) or beats (16b, using @bpm).
# transition: "none" (cut) or any shader name in shaders/transitions/ (crossfade, flash, wipe, dissolve, glitch).
# It blends in from the previous entry during the first <length> of this entry; the first entry fades in from
# black and, when the demo loops, from the last entry.
# Params are passed to the scene (see the comment at the top of each src/scenes/<name>/*Scene.cpp);
# post.<name>=value overrides post settings for this entry
# (exposure, bloom, threshold, knee, radius, chromatic, vignette, grain).
#
# Directives:
#   @bpm 125                       tempo for beat durations and the scenes' beat grid
#   @music placeholder             generated ProTracker song (default); "none" = silence;
#                                  or a module path relative to this folder, e.g. music/track.xm
#
# Available scenes: intro, hstars, pillars, warp, corona, asteroids, rings, canyon, fleet, dreadnought,
#                   supernova, wormhole, galaxy, blackhole, credits
#                   (plus nebula and neongrid, early placeholders kept as small code examples).
# Keep entries in multiples of 16 beats: one pattern of the placeholder song, so scene changes land on
# musical sections. Placeholder instruments: 1 kick, 2 snare, 3 hi-hat, 4 bass, 5 lead.

@bpm   125
@music placeholder

# Departure: title, cruising out through a nebula, jump to hyperspace.
intro       32b   crossfade 2b
hstars      16b   crossfade 2b
pillars     48b   crossfade 2b
warp        16b   crossfade 1b

# Hyperspace exit at a giant star; through its asteroid belt to a ringed giant, down to one of its moons.
corona      32b   flash     1b
asteroids   32b   crossfade 2b
rings       48b   crossfade 2b
canyon      48b   crossfade 2b

# The fleet drops out of hyperspace; the dreadnought up close (low bloom keeps the hull detail readable).
fleet       32b   flash     1b   post.bloom=0.2 post.threshold=2.0
dreadnought 80b   crossfade 2b   post.bloom=0.15 post.threshold=2.5

# The star dies; a wormhole opens onto another galaxy...
supernova   48b   crossfade 2b
wormhole    32b   crossfade 2b
galaxy      64b   crossfade 1b

# ...the black hole at its core, and the credits. The demo then loops back to the title.
blackhole   32b   crossfade 3b
credits     64b   crossfade 3b
